  "content": {
    "objective": "Keep reading numbers advantages continuously as the group changes roles every possession.",
    "setup": "Three attackers push against two defenders at one end; after the possession, the two original defenders become attackers at the other end against a fresh third defender.",
    "organization": "",
    "instructions": [
      "Three attackers push the ball, spacing wide and reading the two defenders.",
      "After a score or stop, the two defenders sprint the other way and become the attack.",
      "A new third defender joins from the sideline to make it three-on-two again.",
      "Continue the cycle continuously for the set duration."
    ],
    "coachingPoints": [
      "Keep spacing wide on every advantage, not bunched in the middle.",
      "Transition mentally as fast as physically — know your new role immediately.",
      "Communicate who is attacking and who is defending at every switch."
    ],
    "commonMistakes": [
      "Standing around after a possession instead of transitioning immediately.",
      "Bunching together instead of using the full width of the floor.",
      "Forcing a play before the numbers advantage is actually clear."
    ],
    "safety": "Keep the full length of the court clear and watch for players crossing paths at the switch.",
